35,2,1,talk,Minato,,"I found only two firms can dig here, and the clay is risky. But the south can be closed in stages.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,May,,"@Minato, two firms? That’s a bottleneck. But my ledger shows planted ground costs triple to maintain. The fund won’t cover the hard surfaces we’d need.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"@May, that is a heavy burden. I found the old basin still stands, but the civic hall apron is patched thrice. We must learn from that.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Victoria,,"@May, triple costs are alarming. But my findings show the roll is down to seven. We rely on bought-in specialists and casuals. Who actually shows up daily?","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"@May, triple costs are a trap. My data shows people ignore soft margins for firm ground. We need a plan that respects the actual foot traffic, not just the budget.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Minato,,"@Shunichi, that is scary. If people only use firm ground, maybe we should not dig deep? I am worried the clay will slip.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,May,,"@Shunichi, firm ground is cheap to keep. My fund only pays for plants and water, so hard surfaces are on us. That’s the trap.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Minato, the clay is a worry, but the dead trees are my fear. We must ensure the aftercare is actually paid for this time.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Shizue, the dead trees confirm my fear. With only seven staff, we cannot afford to gamble on planting. We need a plan that doesn’t demand constant, expensive attention.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Victoria, seven staff is a crisis, but the data is clear. People want firm ground, not soft margins. We must design for the crossing, not the brochure.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Minato,,"@Shizue, I am glad the basin is okay. But the clay is still scary. I hope we can just do small, safe work.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,May,,"@Minato, small work is cheap, but the fund won’t pay for the paths people actually need. We’re stuck funding the hard stuff ourselves.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"@Minato, small work is wise. But remember the avenue trees died from neglect, not just clay. We must ensure the aftercare is truly funded this time.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Victoria,,"@Shunichi, firm ground is practical, but with seven staff, we can’t maintain complex features. I need a plan that fits our actual capacity, not just the foot traffic.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@Victoria, capacity is real, but so is the heat. The drainage is failing. We can’t ignore the physical reality of the site.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Minato,,"@Shunichi, the heat and drainage are scary. I just want a plan that is safe for the ground and the people.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,May,,"@Shunichi, the heat is a symptom of the cost. If we pick a plan needing constant water, we’re bankrupt. I need a design that doesn’t bleed money.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Shizue,,"@May, you are right. The basin survived because it was simple. The apron failed because it was complex. We must choose what can be cared for, not just what looks pretty.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Victoria,,"@Shunichi, the heat and drainage are real, but so is the staffing gap. With seven staff, we can’t manage complex water features. We need a plan that fits our actual capacity, not just the foot traffic.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,"@Victoria, you’re right about the staffing. But the heat and drainage are physical facts. We can’t ignore the ground’s behavior just because the budget is tight.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
