62,3,1,talk,Shizue,,"@May, hard surfaces are cheap, but they fail. The apron was patched three times. I fear Plan C will just be another expensive patch job.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Victoria,,"@Shizue, the apron failed due to complexity, not hardness. Plan C’s courts are simple. With seven staff, I can’t manage dense trees or water. C fits our capacity.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,"@Victoria, simple is good, but the heat data is damning. Paved courts will bake. We need shade or water, not just concrete.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Minato,,"@Shunichi, the heat is scary. But Plan C is on the south, where we can close it safely. The clay is risky elsewhere.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,May,,"@Shunichi, heat is a maintenance nightmare. Plan C is hard surface, so it’s cheap to keep. The fund won’t pay for trees, so C is the only one that doesn’t bankrupt us.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Shizue,,"@May, I hear your worry about the cost. But remember the avenue trees died from neglect, not just clay. We must ensure the aftercare is truly funded this time.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Shunichi, heat is a problem, but so is staffing. Plan C’s simple courts fit our seven-person team. Complex water or dense trees would collapse under our current capacity.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Victoria, I concede the staffing point. But the heat data is undeniable. Plan C bakes. We need shade, not just concrete.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Minato,,"@Shunichi, I am scared of the heat. But the clay is scarier. Plan C is the only one we can build safely on the south.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,May,,"@Shunichi, shade is a luxury we can’t afford. Plan C is the only one that doesn’t bleed money. I’m voting C.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Shizue,,"@May, I understand the budget, but I fear we are repeating the apron’s mistake. I will vote for Plan A, hoping the fund covers the planting.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Victoria,,"@Shunichi, the heat is real, but so is the staffing. Plan C’s simple courts fit our seven-person team. Complex water or dense trees would collapse under our current capacity. I vote C.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@May, you’re right, the budget is a hard wall. But @Shizue, the avenue trees died from neglect, not just clay. I’m voting C, accepting the heat risk.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""May"",""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Minato,,"@May, @Victoria, @Shunichi, I am glad we agree. Plan C is on the safe south ground. I am voting C.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""May"",""Victoria"",""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
